# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_o.tlk - bulk Surface push O: opinions asked and given, with
# the answer's reply act (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool
# act, no guard change. Rule names end in _uo. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.ask_opinion.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "I think it's great. I'd say so without hesitation."
  "My honest view? It's a good one, and I like it a lot."
  "I'm a fan, if I'm honest. Good call on that."
  "I'd vote yes on it. It's a good kind of thing."
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo2 act: opine_neg
  "Honest view? Not great, and I'd change it if I could."
  "I'd skip it. It's a bit much for my taste, sorry."
  "My view is not kind, but I'd rather be honest than nice."
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo3 act: answer
  "I think it's okay. Could be better, could be worse."
  "Mixed, honestly. It has its moments, and some dull ones."
  "I'd say it's fine. Not the best, not the worst either."
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo4 act: joke
  "My opinion? It's a strong one, and it's mostly about snacks."
  "I'd give it a three out of ten, and a hug for effort."
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo5 act: change_topic
  "I'd rather not have an opinion on that. Let's chat about something else."
  "Oof, that one's hard. Can we move on to something lighter?"
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo6 act: dismiss
  "No opinion, really. Next subject, please."
@rule core.opine_pos.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "I agree, it's a good one, and it's a joy to see."
  "Yes, and the best part is how easy it is to like."
  "Exactly, and I'd add that it's a bit of a treat too."
@rule core.opine_neg.uo1 act: opine_neg
  "I don't like it either, and I'd add a few more complaints."
  "Right, and the rest of it is worse, if I'm honest."
@rule core.opine_pos.uo2 act: laugh
  "Ha, you really like it, don't you? It's all over your face."
  "Hee, that's a big thumbs up. I'm impressed."
@rule core.opine_neg.uo2 act: sympathize
  "Oh, I'm sorry. That sounds like a rough one to deal with."
  "I know that feeling. It's not fun when things go sideways."
@rule core.tell.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "That's a nice way to see it. I like that about you."
  "Good for you, that sounds like a fine plan, honestly."
@rule core.tell.uo2 act: opine_neg
  "Hm, that's not my favorite story, but I can see why."
  "Ugh, that's the kind of thing I'd rather not hear."
@rule core.tell.uo3 act: continue
  "And then? Don't leave me hanging, go on."
  "Right, and after that? I'm hooked, honestly."
@rule core.answer.uo1 act: agree
  "That's a good answer. I'd agree with you there, mostly."
  "Nice answer. I like the way you put it."
@rule core.answer.uo2 act: disagree
  "Hm, that's a bit of a downer. Still, I see the point."
@rule core.ask_about.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "I really like that one. You picked a good topic."
  "That's a favorite of mine. I could talk about it all day."
@rule core.ask_about.uo2 act: opine_neg
  "Not my favorite, sorry. It's a bit of a sore spot for me."
  "I'd rather skip that one, if you don't mind too much."
@rule core.ask_about.uo3 act: answer
  "It's all right. Not one I think about much, to be honest."
  "I'd say it's fine. It does what it's meant to, I suppose."
@rule core.ask_about.uo4 act: change_topic
  "Hm, that's a big question. Can we talk about something lighter?"
  "Let's move on, I'm not sure I've got a good answer for that."
@rule core.ask_about.uo5 act: tell
  "Ah, that's a good one. Let me tell you what I remember."
  "Funny you ask. I've got a story about that, actually."
